        H('III. PROPOSED SOLUTION'),S('A. Component Architecture'),
        ('arch',),C('Fig. 1. Component architecture and named formal data interfaces.'),
        'The browser owns presentation and playback. Starlette owns model loading, jobs, validation and result evidence. A shared BERT encoder serves the direct DFA predictor and the small grammar or semantic-plan heads. The formal component accepts typed objects, not raw English. It supplies automata construction, simulation, equivalence, CFG parsing and symbolic compiler checks. A separate rendering component consumes these checked structures and their traces. Dataset manifests and model fingerprints provide the artifact boundary.',
        'This organization avoids a second language interpreter in the renderer. Changing an English description invokes the selected BERT predictor. Changing a test word reuses the formal object and computes another trace. The SVG geometry, node styles, edge routing and playback controls remain the same when a different prediction architecture is selected. The neural and formal components share a versioned JSON DFA contract, so an improved interpreter need not redesign the final visual representation.',
