        'The plan dataset contains 2,914 canonical DFA languages. It annotates 6,274 prior V3 rows with copyable equivalent plans and adds generated supervision; one prior row has no supported copyable annotation. Languages inherit protected prior split roles, and new identities use a deterministic hash split. A retired challenge development subset contributes supervision only when its canonical language belongs to training. Assertions enforce one partition per language.',
