        'The active V3 direct model achieves 562/641 exact first predictions (87.68%) and 599/641 successes within five (93.45%) on its generated test set. In an earlier matched 379-example comparison, expansion improved first-candidate equivalence from 62.53% to 90.24%. Those scores concern different evaluation sets and must not be concatenated into a single learning curve. A subsequent robust direct fine-tune was rejected because its original validation regression and product failures violated the selection gates.',
