        'Preserving presentation does not mean freezing content. A suffix of length four can require more states than a one-symbol suffix. A longer accepted input can revisit a loop several times without adding graph states. The UI must show both facts accurately. Tests therefore compare the displayed state and transition counts with the current formal object, and compare playback with its trace. This guards against both a makeshift fixed diagram and an incorrectly input-dependent state count.',
