        'The original grammar generator covers matching counts, balanced delimiters, ordered blocks, palindromes and arbitrary words over selected symbols from a, b, x, y, 0 and 1. It also includes canonical arithmetic grammars as known fixtures. Its 1,299 examples contain 123 unique production identities. The model is a learned production-token decoder, not a retrieval table of English patterns.',
        'The robust augmentation contributes 456 descriptions. Merging includes deduplication and removal of protected training identities, so 1,299 plus 456 is not the final row count. The robust dataset has 1,652 rows and 119 grammar identities. Arithmetic, ambiguous addition and compiler grammars are intentionally known training fixtures. Their product behavior is tested, but it is not held-out grammar discovery.',
        'The original grammar dataset is stored at artifacts/bert-grammar/dataset.jsonl. A pooled-feature pilot dataset also exists at artifacts/bert-grammar-pilot/dataset.jsonl. The robust merged file is artifacts/grammar-robust/dataset.jsonl. The augmentation is data/generated/grammar-robust.jsonl. These are project-generated corpora without a separate external dataset license or public download URL.',
        'Mixed challenge v1 contains 100 DFA, 38 CFG and 27 compiler requests. Its reserved test contains 23 DFA, 14 CFG and nine compiler cases. It distinguishes wording interpretation, structure generation, unsupported state bounds and downstream visualization. It has now been inspected and partly used through eligible development cases, so future work should treat it as retired regression evidence rather than an untouched test.',
        'Plan comparison v2 contains 254 unique formal language identities outside the new plan training split. Its descriptions use a distinct wrapper and selected held-out wording styles. Validation has 134 cases; test has 120. Targets include cases above the direct head\'s capacity, so the analysis also reports a matched subset with at most eight states and no more than 64 baseline tokens. The file is frozen by SHA-256 before either model predicts it.',
