        'The new and direct systems differ in architecture, output representation and training supervision. The comparison evaluates the full new local approach. It cannot isolate representation as the only cause of improvement. Timing is sequential on the same machine with two CPU threads, but background load, cache warmth and Python overhead remain. There is one seed, no confidence calibration and no independent human evaluation. These limitations are part of the reported result.'
